    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YUwbTNFP92MbconEgCJZPM)_\n\n**What:** `sp-globals` (`libraries/modules/base/sp-globals.el`, doc `docs/tangles/base/sp-globals.org`) is now the one file for my most important settings, locations included.\n\n- **`sp-paths` is gone as a module.** Its content is in `sp-globals`, which says (commentary and doc) that it holds what should have been `sp-paths` as well, combined for simplicity and brevity. `(provide 'sp-paths)` stays, so an old `(require 'sp-paths)` still works. `init.el`, the four profiles, `sp-env`, `sp-org-lint`, `sp-org-normalise`, `docs/main.org`, `load-order.org`, the README and the run-emacs-modular skill now point at `sp-globals`.\n- **Moved in, with the same defaults:**\n  - `auth-sources` (`sp-auth-sources`).\n  - `sp-bibliography`, `sp-bib-notes`, `sp-citar-note`.\n  - The four `sp-dashboard-*` privacy options.\n  - `sia-hunspell-dictionaries`, plus the new `sp-ispell-program`.\n  - Prompts, bells and dialogs: `sp-confirm-kill-emacs`, `sp-confirm-kill-processes`, `sp-ring-bell-function`, `sp-visible-bell`, `sp-use-dialog-box`, `sp-use-file-dialog`.\n  - `sp-backup-directory` and `sp-create-lockfiles`.\n  - `sp-calendar-week-start-day`.\n  - `sp-persistent-scratch`, `sp-scratch-default-dir`.\n  - The folders `sp-bibtex-dir`, `sp-scratch-save-dir`, `sp-treemacs-root`, `sp-tab-inbox-dir`, `sp-emoji-font-install-dir`, `sp-trails-chrome-history`.\n  - New and `nil` (nothing changes until filled in): `sp-user-full-name`, `sp-user-mail-address`.\n- **Pointers:** every place a setting used to live has a `;; Moved to `sp-globals': ...` comment, in the `.el` and in the doc, and the doc prose links to `sp-globals`.\n- **Left where they are, as asked:** `sp-headless-host`, `sp-defer-late-modules`, per-package `:custom`, platform settings, values derived from a path. The default font and the theme also stay (`sp-fonts`, `sp-themes`).\n\n**Behaviour changes to know about:**\n- The `setq` settings (bells, dialogs, confirmations, lock files, backup folder, week start, `auth-sources`) now apply at startup, not when their old module loads.\n- `sp-ispell-program` is a name, looked up in `sp-spelling` with `executable-find` as before (not at startup, because the macOS `PATH` is only complete after `sp-env`).\n- `sp-tab-inbox-dir` is built from `sp-notes-dir` (same as `org-directory`), so it no longer needs Org loaded. `sp-emoji-font-install-dir` is built from `sp-data-home` (same folder).\n- `sp-trails-chrome-history` kept its name and default; only its definition moved.\n\n**Not tested:** no Emacs here. Brackets are balanced; every doc still tangles to its `.el` (the same 15 doc/`.el` mismatches as on `main`, none of them new); `set-defcustom-group.py --check` reports only the three `sp-collection-query-tables` files that it already reported on `main`. No CHANGELOG line, to avoid more conflicts on the \"Open pull requests\" set.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01PF79fi4scSSid1V5FvNkEF",
